Widescreen object range: Crash 2 spawns objects for the widened view, not
just the 4:3 one.

The edge popping that NOTES "Widescreen, parts 4-7" could not remove is object
ACTIVATION, not rendering. Crash 2 creates and removes enemies, crates and
platforms from two per-node lists on each camera path entity, authored for the
4:3 frustum (0x13C: visible from this node, 0x13B: last visible at this node).
The camera update walks the path one node at a time through func_8001A13C,
which queues kills and spawns in a 12-byte queue at 0x8006302C (count at
[gp+0x23C]) that func_8001A23C then carries out. Any wider view therefore
shows objects appearing and vanishing at its edges.

crash2_wide_spawn.h (new) widens that in time: at node n an object is wanted if
the original lists show it anywhere within [n-k, n+k]. The game's call runs
unchanged; at its return the hook reads the camera entity's rows the way the
engine's accessor (0x80031AE8) does, rebuilds each nearby object's original
presence from all its rows in the path, and acts only on objects the window
wants and the original does not: their queue action becomes spawn (kept alive,
or spawned early). Objects neither wants that are still alive are killed again.
The original's own objects are never touched; with k = 0 nothing changes.

Level data is reference-counted per node (load lists 0x208/0x209), so an
object may spawn early only if no load row lies between here and its original
spawn node, and is kept late only if no unload row lies between its original
kill node and here - it never outlives, or runs ahead of, the data it uses. A
spawn that still fails returns an error the game already handles and is
retried at the next node. Objects whose rows do not open and close inside the
path (their state depends on which end the path was entered from) are left to
the game. The queue has no bounds check in the game; the hook never appends
past 45 of its 53 entries. After a state load or a window change (the Home
menu's aspect, a 4:3 FMV) the next node re-checks every queued object.

PSX_CRASH2_WIDE_SPAWN=N (nodes at 16:9, scaled by the live widescreen margin,
off by default). Every code word it depends on is checked first. The c2_spawn
debug command changes it live and reports counters; the heartbeat carries them
as "wide_spawn". Checked against a model of the game's queue with the real
executable as guest RAM (tuning/wide_spawn_sim).

No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake; overlay shards are unaffected.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/runtime/src/crash2_wide_spawn.h
@@ -0,0 +1,459 @@
+/* SCUS-94154 only: spawn objects for the widened view, not just the 4:3 one.
+ *
+ * Crash 2 does not decide per frame which objects exist. Each camera path
+ * entity carries two per-node lists, authored offline for the 4:3 frustum:
+ *
+ *   0x13C  "draw list B"  entities that become visible AT that node (forward)
+ *   0x13B  "draw list A"  entities last visible at that node (forward)
+ *
+ * The camera update (0x80020200..0x80020830) walks the path one node at a time
+ * and calls func_8001A13C(entity, node<<8, dir) per node: forward (dir 2) it
+ * queues a kill for A(n-1) and a spawn for B(n); backward (dir 1) a kill for
+ * B(n+1) and a spawn for A(n). func_8001A054 puts those in a 12-byte queue at
+ * 0x8006302C ({value, object, action}, count at [gp+0x23C], last action per
+ * entity wins) and func_8001A23C carries it out: 0x13C spawns the entity
+ * (func_80019098), 0x13B kills its object (func_80019BBC). Entering a path or
+ * jumping along it marks every queued entity 0x13B (func_8001A014) and replays
+ * the path node by node from the nearer end.
+ *
+ * So objects appear and vanish exactly at the node where the 4:3 view starts
+ * or stops seeing them; widen the view and they pop at its edges. This hook
+ * widens that in TIME instead: at node n an object is wanted if the original
+ * lists would show it at any node within [n-k, n+k].
+ *
+ * How, without touching the game's own decisions:
+ *
+ *   - The game's call runs unchanged. At its return (jr $ra is a hook point)
+ *     the rows near n are read straight from the entity, the way 0x80031AE8
+ *     reads them, and each nearby entity's ORIGINAL presence at n is rebuilt
+ *     from all its rows in this path. That rebuilt presence is exactly the
+ *     game's own state: every step it takes is one row's worth of it, and a
+ *     path entry replays it from an end. Entities the original wants are left
+ *     entirely to the original. Entities it does not want but the window does
+ *     are spawned early or kept alive; entities neither wants but that are
+ *     alive - ours, from an earlier node - are killed again. With k = 0 the
+ *     window is the original, so nothing is ever changed.
+ *
+ *   - Level data is reference-counted per node too (load lists 0x208/0x209,
+ *     func_800217F8 -> func_80021900). An object must never outlive, or run
+ *     ahead of, the data it uses. So:
+ *       early spawn only if no load row lies between here and the node where
+ *         the original spawns it - its data was already requested, exactly as
+ *         the original relies on;
+ *       late keep only if no unload row lies between the node where the
+ *         original killed it and here - at the first unload it dies in the same
+ *         update, just as the original's object did.
+ *     A spawn that still fails (object pool full, code not resident) returns
+ *     an error, the game drops the queue entry, and the next node retries.
+ *
+ *   - The queue has no bounds check in the game. Its region ends where other
+ *     data begins (0x800632AC: 53 entries); this never appends past
+ *     C2WS_Q_CAP - C2WS_Q_HEADROOM, and simply does less when that is near.
+ *
+ *   - After a state load, or when the window changes (aspect switched in the
+ *     Home menu, a 4:3 FMV), the next node re-checks every queued entity, not
+ *     just the nearby ones, so nothing we kept can be left behind.
+ *
+ * Off unless PSX_CRASH2_WIDE_SPAWN > 0. The window is 0 - retire only - at 4:3
+ * and on frames presented 4:3 (same gate as crash2_wide_bbox.h). Every code
+ * word it depends on is checked first; any mismatch leaves the game alone. */
+
+#define C2WS_FN          0x8001A13Cu  /* queue one node's draw-list rows        */
+#define C2WS_RA_STEP     0x8002052Cu  /* return from the per-node walk call     */
+#define C2WS_RA_ENTRY_0  0x80020424u  /* return from path entry at node 0 (fwd)  */
+#define C2WS_RA_ENTRY_L  0x80020470u  /* return from path entry at the last node */
+#define C2WS_Q_BASE      0x8006302Cu
+#define C2WS_Q_COUNT     0x8005F3B8u  /* [gp+0x23C], gp = 0x8005F17C            */
+#define C2WS_Q_CAP       53u          /* 0x800632AC - 0x8006302C = 0x280 bytes   */
+#define C2WS_Q_HEADROOM  8u
+#define C2WS_KILL        0x13Bu
+#define C2WS_SPAWN       0x13Cu
+#define C2WS_P_DRAW_A    0x13B
+#define C2WS_P_DRAW_B    0x13C
+#define C2WS_P_LOAD_A    0x208
+#define C2WS_P_LOAD_B    0x209
+#define C2WS_MAX_ROWS    256
+#define C2WS_MAX_CAND    96
+#define C2WS_MAX_EVENTS  48
+#define C2WS_MAX_K       8
+
+#ifndef C2WS_R32
+extern uint32_t psx_read_word(uint32_t a);
+extern uint16_t psx_read_half(uint32_t a);
+extern uint8_t  psx_read_byte(uint32_t a);
+extern void     psx_write_word(uint32_t a, uint32_t v);
+#define C2WS_R32(a)    psx_read_word(a)
+#define C2WS_R16(a)    psx_read_half(a)
+#define C2WS_R8(a)     psx_read_byte(a)
+#define C2WS_W32(a, v) psx_write_word((a), (v))
+#endif
+
+typedef struct { int node; uint32_t vals; int count; } C2wsRow;
+typedef struct { int n; C2wsRow r[C2WS_MAX_ROWS]; } C2wsProp;
+typedef struct { int node; int on; } C2wsEvent;
+typedef struct { uint32_t key, value; int n; C2wsEvent e[C2WS_MAX_EVENTS]; } C2wsCand;
+
+static int c2ws_base_k = -1;          /* PSX_CRASH2_WIDE_SPAWN; -1 = unread     */
+static int c2ws_sig = -1;             /* code words: -1 unchecked, 0 bad, 1 ok  */
+static int c2ws_last_k = -1;          /* window used at the previous node       */
+static int c2ws_full_pass = 1;        /* re-check every queued entity next node */
+static struct { int armed; uint32_t ra, cam; int node, dir, k; } c2ws_call;
+static unsigned long long c2ws_arrivals, c2ws_early, c2ws_kept, c2ws_retired,
+                          c2ws_unsafe_load, c2ws_unsafe_unload, c2ws_full,
+                          c2ws_bad;
+
+static int c2ws_is_ram(uint32_t a) { return a >= 0x80000000u && a < 0x801FFFF0u; }
+
+/* One property's rows, read the way 0x80031AE8 reads them: binary search of
+ * the 8-byte headers at entity+16 (count at +12), falling back along the
+ * entity+8 chain; data at entity+12+offset; flag 0x40 = per-row counts
+ * (uint16[n]) else one shared count; flag 0x20 = an int16 node per row;
+ * values start 4-aligned after that. Returns 0 (rows or none), -1 for
+ * anything this does not understand - the caller then leaves the game alone. */
+static int c2ws_prop(uint32_t ent, int id, C2wsProp *out)
+{
+    out->n = 0;
+    for (int depth = 0; ent != 0u && depth < 4; depth++) {
+        if (!c2ws_is_ram(ent)) return -1;
+        int lo = 0, hi = (int16_t)C2WS_R16(ent + 12u) - 1;
+        uint32_t hdr = 0u;
+        if (hi > 512) return -1;
+        while (lo <= hi) {
+            const int mid = (lo + hi) >> 1;
+            const uint32_t h = ent + 16u + (uint32_t)mid * 8u;
+            const int hid = (int16_t)C2WS_R16(h);
+            if (hid == id) { hdr = h; break; }
+            if (hid < id) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1;
+        }
+        if (hdr == 0u) { ent = C2WS_R32(ent + 8u); continue; }
+        const uint32_t data = ent + 12u + C2WS_R16(hdr + 2u);
+        const unsigned flags = C2WS_R8(hdr + 4u);
+        const unsigned esize = C2WS_R8(hdr + 5u);
+        const int nrows = C2WS_R16(hdr + 6u);
+        if (!(flags & 0x20u) || esize != 4u || nrows > C2WS_MAX_ROWS) return -1;
+        uint32_t counts = 0u, metas;
+        int common = 0;
+        if (flags & 0x40u) { counts = data; metas = data + 2u * (uint32_t)nrows; }
+        else { common = C2WS_R16(data); metas = data + 2u; }
+        const uint32_t vals = (metas + 2u * (uint32_t)nrows + 3u) & ~3u;
+        uint32_t off = 0u;
+        for (int i = 0; i < nrows; i++) {
+            const int c = counts ? (int)C2WS_R16(counts + 2u * (uint32_t)i) : common;
+            if (c < 0 || c > 256) return -1;
+            out->r[i].node = (int16_t)C2WS_R16(metas + 2u * (uint32_t)i);
+            out->r[i].vals = vals + off * 4u;
+            out->r[i].count = c;
+            off += (uint32_t)c;
+        }
+        if (!c2ws_is_ram(vals + off * 4u)) return -1;
+        out->n = nrows;
+        return 0;
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+
+/* Non-empty row at exactly this node (the accessor's exact-match mode). */
+static int c2ws_row_at(const C2wsProp *p, int node)
+{
+    for (int i = 0; i < p->n; i++)
+        if (p->r[i].node == node) return p->r[i].count > 0;
+    return 0;
+}
+
+/* Presence under the ORIGINAL lists: B(s) makes an entity present from s,
+ * A(e) absent from e+1. At one node a start outranks an end (the game queues
+ * the kill first and the spawn second, and the last action wins). Before its
+ * first event it is present iff that event is an end - it was carried in. */
+static int c2ws_present(const C2wsCand *c, int x)
+{
+    if (c->n == 0) return 0;
+    int on = !c->e[0].on;
+    for (int i = 0; i < c->n && c->e[i].node <= x; i++) on = c->e[i].on;
+    return on;
+}
+
+static int c2ws_add_cand(C2wsCand *cand, int *ncand, uint32_t key)
+{
+    for (int i = 0; i < *ncand; i++) if (cand[i].key == key) return i;
+    if (*ncand >= C2WS_MAX_CAND) return -1;
+    cand[*ncand].key = key;
+    cand[*ncand].value = 0u;
+    cand[*ncand].n = 0;
+    return (*ncand)++;
+}
+
+/* Queue index for this entity, -1 none, -2 queue state not understood. */
+static int c2ws_q_find(uint32_t key)
+{
+    const uint32_t n = C2WS_R32(C2WS_Q_COUNT);
+    if (n > C2WS_Q_CAP) return -2;
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < n; i++)
+        if ((C2WS_R32(C2WS_Q_BASE + i * 12u) & 0x00FFFF00u) == key) return (int)i;
+    return -1;
+}
+
+/* func_8001A054 for one value: rewrite an existing entry, or append one. */
+static int c2ws_q_set(uint32_t value, uint32_t action, int idx)
+{
+    if (idx >= 0) {
+        C2WS_W32(C2WS_Q_BASE + (uint32_t)idx * 12u, value);
+        C2WS_W32(C2WS_Q_BASE + (uint32_t)idx * 12u + 8u, action);
+        return 1;
+    }
+    const uint32_t n = C2WS_R32(C2WS_Q_COUNT);
+    if (n + 1u > C2WS_Q_CAP - C2WS_Q_HEADROOM) return 0;
+    C2WS_W32(C2WS_Q_BASE + n * 12u, value);
+    C2WS_W32(C2WS_Q_BASE + n * 12u + 4u, 0u);
+    C2WS_W32(C2WS_Q_BASE + n * 12u + 8u, action);
+    C2WS_W32(C2WS_Q_COUNT, n + 1u);
+    return 1;
+}
+
+/* The load / unload row a given arrival processes (func_800217F8): forward
+ * arrival j loads LA(j) and unloads LB(j-1); backward loads LB(j) and unloads
+ * LA(j+1). */
+static int c2ws_loads_at(const C2wsProp *la, const C2wsProp *lb, int j, int d)
+{
+    return d > 0 ? c2ws_row_at(la, j) : c2ws_row_at(lb, j);
+}
+static int c2ws_unloads_at(const C2wsProp *la, const C2wsProp *lb, int j, int d)
+{
+    return d > 0 ? c2ws_row_at(lb, j - 1) : c2ws_row_at(la, j + 1);
+}
+
+/* Whether the window wants an entity the original does not, at node n. */
+static int c2ws_window_wants(const C2wsCand *c, const C2wsProp *la,
+                             const C2wsProp *lb, int n, int d, int k)
+{
+    /* Ahead in the direction of travel: spawn early, if its data was already
+     * requested (no load row up to the node where the original spawns it). */
+    for (int t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
+        const int x = n + d * t;
+        if (!c2ws_present(c, x)) continue;
+        for (int j = n + d; ; j += d) {
+            if (c2ws_loads_at(la, lb, j, d)) { c2ws_unsafe_load++; goto behind; }
+            if (j == x) break;
+        }
+        return 1;
+    }
+behind:
+    /* Behind: keep alive, unless something was unloaded since the node where
+     * the original killed it. */
+    for (int t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
+        const int x = n - d * t;
+        if (!c2ws_present(c, x)) continue;
+        for (int j = x + d; ; j += d) {
+            if (c2ws_unloads_at(la, lb, j, d)) { c2ws_unsafe_unload++; return 0; }
+            if (j == n) break;
+        }
+        return 1;
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static void c2ws_apply(uint32_t cam, int n, int dir, int k)
+{
+    static C2wsProp a, b, la, lb;
+    static C2wsCand cand[C2WS_MAX_CAND];
+    int ncand = 0;
+    if (c2ws_prop(cam, C2WS_P_DRAW_A, &a) < 0 || c2ws_prop(cam, C2WS_P_DRAW_B, &b) < 0 ||
+        c2ws_prop(cam, C2WS_P_LOAD_A, &la) < 0 || c2ws_prop(cam, C2WS_P_LOAD_B, &lb) < 0) {
+        c2ws_bad++;
+        return;
+    }
+    const int d = dir == 2 ? 1 : -1;
+    const int reach = k > 0 ? k : 0;
+
+    /* Candidates: every entity with a row close enough for the window to
+     * change its state here, and - after a load or a window change - every
+     * entity in the queue. */
+    for (int pass = 0; pass < 2; pass++) {
+        const C2wsProp *p = pass ? &b : &a;
+        for (int i = 0; i < p->n; i++) {
+            if (p->r[i].node < n - reach - 1 || p->r[i].node > n + reach + 1) continue;
+            for (int j = 0; j < p->r[i].count; j++)
+                c2ws_add_cand(cand, &ncand,
+                              C2WS_R32(p->r[i].vals + 4u * (uint32_t)j) & 0x00FFFF00u);
+        }
+    }
+    if (c2ws_full_pass) {
+        const uint32_t qn = C2WS_R32(C2WS_Q_COUNT);
+        if (qn > C2WS_Q_CAP) { c2ws_bad++; return; }
+        for (uint32_t i = 0; i < qn; i++)
+            c2ws_add_cand(cand, &ncand, C2WS_R32(C2WS_Q_BASE + i * 12u) & 0x00FFFF00u);
+        c2ws_full_pass = 0;
+    }
+    /* One pass over all of this path's rows builds every candidate's events. */
+    for (int pass = 0; pass < 2; pass++) {
+        const C2wsProp *p = pass ? &b : &a;
+        for (int i = 0; i < p->n; i++)
+            for (int j = 0; j < p->r[i].count; j++) {
+                const uint32_t v = C2WS_R32(p->r[i].vals + 4u * (uint32_t)j);
+                for (int c = 0; c < ncand; c++) {
+                    if (cand[c].key != (v & 0x00FFFF00u)) continue;
+                    if (cand[c].n < C2WS_MAX_EVENTS) {
+                        cand[c].value = v;
+                        cand[c].e[cand[c].n].node = pass ? p->r[i].node : p->r[i].node + 1;
+                        cand[c].e[cand[c].n].on = pass;
+                        cand[c].n++;
+                    }
+                    break;
+                }
+            }
+    }
+
+    for (int c = 0; c < ncand; c++) {
+        C2wsCand *cd = &cand[c];
+        if (cd->n == 0) continue;            /* no rows in this path: not ours to judge */
+        for (int i = 1; i < cd->n; i++) {    /* by node, ends before starts */
+            const C2wsEvent t = cd->e[i];
+            int j = i - 1;
+            while (j >= 0 && (cd->e[j].node > t.node ||
+                              (cd->e[j].node == t.node && cd->e[j].on > t.on))) {
+                cd->e[j + 1] = cd->e[j];
+                j--;
+            }
+            cd->e[j + 1] = t;
+        }
+        /* An interval must open and close inside this path. Replaying from
+         * the start never spawns an entity whose first row here is an end,
+         * and replaying from the far end never spawns one whose last row is
+         * a start, so for those the game's state depends on which end the
+         * path was entered from - which the rows cannot tell us. Well-formed
+         * data has none (visible at node 0 is a B(0) row, visible at the
+         * last node an A row there); anything else is left to the game. */
+        if (cd->e[0].on == 0 || cd->e[cd->n - 1].on == 1) continue;
+        if (c2ws_present(cd, n)) continue;   /* the original's, entirely */
+        const int want = c2ws_window_wants(cd, &la, &lb, n, d, reach);
+        const int qi = c2ws_q_find(cd->key);
+        if (qi == -2) { c2ws_bad++; return; }
+        const uint32_t act = qi >= 0 ? C2WS_R32(C2WS_Q_BASE + (uint32_t)qi * 12u + 8u) : 0u;
+        if (!want) {
+            /* Alive (or about to spawn) although neither the original nor the
+             * window wants it: one we kept or spawned earlier. */
+            if (qi >= 0 && act != C2WS_KILL) {
+                c2ws_q_set(C2WS_R32(C2WS_Q_BASE + (uint32_t)qi * 12u), C2WS_KILL, qi);
+                c2ws_retired++;
+            }
+        } else if (qi >= 0) {
+            if (act == C2WS_KILL) {          /* the original just killed it: keep */
+                c2ws_q_set(C2WS_R32(C2WS_Q_BASE + (uint32_t)qi * 12u), C2WS_SPAWN, qi);
+                c2ws_kept++;
+            }
+        } else if (c2ws_q_set(cd->value, C2WS_SPAWN, -1)) {
+            c2ws_early++;
+        } else {
+            c2ws_full++;
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+static int c2ws_code_ok(CPUState *cpu)
+{
+    if (c2ws_sig < 0) {
+        c2ws_sig =
+            cpu->read_word(0x8001A13Cu) == 0x27BDFFC0u &&   /* func_8001A13C prologue     */
+            cpu->read_word(0x8001A158u) == 0x3405013Cu &&   /* ori a1,0x13C                */
+            cpu->read_word(0x8001A16Cu) == 0x3405013Bu &&   /* ori a1,0x13B                */
+            cpu->read_word(0x8001A19Cu) == 0x0C00C6BAu &&   /* jal 0x80031AE8              */
+            cpu->read_word(0x8001A1BCu) == 0x0C006815u &&   /* jal 0x8001A054              */
+            cpu->read_word(0x8001A078u) == 0x8F82023Cu &&   /* queue count at gp+0x23C     */
+            cpu->read_word(0x8001A08Cu) == 0x3C088006u &&   /* queue base hi               */
+            cpu->read_word(0x8001A090u) == 0x2508302Cu &&   /* queue base lo 0x302C        */
+            cpu->read_word(0x8001A2DCu) == 0x3402013Bu &&   /* flush: 0x13B = kill         */
+            cpu->read_word(0x8001A2E4u) == 0x3402013Cu &&   /*        0x13C = spawn        */
+            cpu->read_word(0x8002041Cu) == 0x0C00684Fu &&   /* the three call sites        */
+            cpu->read_word(0x80020468u) == 0x0C00684Fu &&
+            cpu->read_word(0x80020524u) == 0x0C00684Fu &&
+            cpu->read_word(0x800204C8u) == 0x0C0085FEu &&   /* load lists before draw lists */
+            cpu->read_word(0x80021814u) == 0x34050208u &&   /* load lists 0x208/0x209      */
+            cpu->read_word(0x80021828u) == 0x34050209u &&
+            cpu->read_word(0x80031AE8u) == 0x27BDFFF8u &&   /* the property accessor       */
+            cpu->read_word(0x80049BA8u) == 0x3C1C8006u &&   /* gp = 0x8005F17C             */
+            cpu->read_word(0x80049BACu) == 0x279CF17Cu;
+    }
+    return c2ws_sig == 1;
+}
+
+/* The window for this frame's widening. The launcher's value is for 16:9
+ * (85 px revealed per side); 14:9 reveals half that, 21:9 more. 0 when the
+ * frame is not widened - which still retires anything kept earlier. */
+static int c2ws_window(void)
+{
+    GpuWsDebug ws;
+    gpu_ws_get_debug(&ws);
+    if (ws.present_native_43) return 0;
+    if (!((ws.mode == 1 && ws.active) || (ws.mode == 2 && ws.nw_extra > 0))) return 0;
+    const int margin = ws.x_margin > 0 ? ws.x_margin : 85;
+    int k = (c2ws_base_k * margin + 42) / 85;
+    if (k < 1) k = 1;
+    return k > C2WS_MAX_K ? C2WS_MAX_K : k;
+}
+
+void crash2_wide_spawn_note_restore(void)
+{
+    c2ws_call.armed = 0;
+    c2ws_full_pass = 1;
+}
+
+void crash2_wide_spawn_control(int k, int reset)
+{
+    if (k >= 0) {
+        c2ws_base_k = k > C2WS_MAX_K ? C2WS_MAX_K : k;
+        c2ws_full_pass = 1;
+    }
+    if (reset) {
+        c2ws_arrivals = c2ws_early = c2ws_kept = c2ws_retired = 0;
+        c2ws_unsafe_load = c2ws_unsafe_unload = c2ws_full = c2ws_bad = 0;
+    }
+}
+
+void crash2_wide_spawn_stats(unsigned long long out[8], int *base_k, int *k, int *sig)
+{
+    out[0] = c2ws_arrivals;  out[1] = c2ws_early;          out[2] = c2ws_kept;
+    out[3] = c2ws_retired;   out[4] = c2ws_unsafe_load;    out[5] = c2ws_unsafe_unload;
+    out[6] = c2ws_full;      out[7] = c2ws_bad;
+    if (base_k) *base_k = c2ws_base_k < 0 ? 0 : c2ws_base_k;
+    if (k) *k = c2ws_last_k < 0 ? 0 : c2ws_last_k;
+    if (sig) *sig = c2ws_sig;
+}
+
+static void crash2_wide_spawn(CPUState *cpu, uint32_t pc)
+{
+    if (pc == C2WS_FN) {
+        const uint32_t ra = cpu->gpr[31];
+        c2ws_call.armed = 0;
+        if (c2ws_base_k < 0) {
+            const char *e = getenv("PSX_CRASH2_WIDE_SPAWN");
+            const int v = e ? atoi(e) : 0;
+            c2ws_base_k = v < 0 ? 0 : (v > C2WS_MAX_K ? C2WS_MAX_K : v);
+        }
+        if (c2ws_base_k == 0) return;
+        if (ra != C2WS_RA_STEP && ra != C2WS_RA_ENTRY_0 && ra != C2WS_RA_ENTRY_L) return;
+        if (!c2ws_code_ok(cpu)) return;
+        const int k = c2ws_window();
+        if (k != c2ws_last_k) {
+            c2ws_full_pass = 1;
+            if (k > 0)
+                fprintf(stdout, "psxrecomp: widescreen object range: %d camera "
+                                "node%s either side (crash2_wide_spawn)\n",
+                        k, k == 1 ? "" : "s");
+        }
+        c2ws_last_k = k;
+        c2ws_call.armed = 1;
+        c2ws_call.ra = ra;
+        c2ws_call.cam = cpu->gpr[4];
+        c2ws_call.node = (int32_t)cpu->gpr[5] >> 8;
+        c2ws_call.dir = (int)cpu->gpr[6];
+        c2ws_call.k = k;
+        return;
+    }
+    if (!c2ws_call.armed || pc != c2ws_call.ra) return;
+    c2ws_call.armed = 0;
+    /* The caller keeps the camera entity in $s5 across the call; anything
+     * else means this is not the return we armed for. */
+    if (cpu->gpr[21] != c2ws_call.cam || !c2ws_is_ram(c2ws_call.cam)) return;
+    if (c2ws_call.dir != 1 && c2ws_call.dir != 2) return;
+    c2ws_arrivals++;
+    c2ws_apply(c2ws_call.cam, c2ws_call.node, c2ws_call.dir, c2ws_call.k);
+}
